data: {"id":"chatcmpl-ecaeeae6-ffe7-4ed6-8022-f25e7898ee05","object":"chat.completion.chunk","created":1795544954,"model":"gemini-4-carbon","choices":[{"index":0,"delta":{"reasoning_content":"Implemented checks for transaction IDs (R14) across record types, including a zero transaction ID check (R13). Added key validation (R15) for PUT, DELETE, and READ records, enforcing length (1-32 bytes) and ASCII range (0x21-0x7E) restrictions.\n\nImplemented value validation (R16) for PUT and READ records (when the flag is 1), enforcing ASCII range (0x20-0x7E) for non-zero lengths. Implemented validation (R16a) for SAVEPOINT and ROLLBACK names, ensuring they are single ASCII characters within the range 0x21-0x7E. Implemented duplicate transaction ID check (R17) for BEGIN records using the `seenTxns` set.\n\n\n"},"finish_reason":null}],"usage":null}

data: {"id":"chatcmpl-ecaeeae6-ffe7-4ed6-8022-f25e7898ee05","object":"chat.completion.chunk","created":1795544954,"model":"gemini-4-carbon","choices":[{"index":0,"delta":{"reasoning_content":"The `seenTxns` set tracks transaction IDs from accepted `BEGIN` records, added during record processing (R20) after limit checks (R18). This design cleanly reflects that a transaction is open from its `BEGIN` acceptance. Examining rule R18, a `TOO_MANY_OPEN` exception terminates recovery immediately, validating this approach. Rule R19 ensures an open transaction exists via `TXN_NOT_OPEN` before processing subsequent records. R19a enforces the write limit.\n\n\n"},"finish_reason":null}],"usage":null}

